1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:03,115
What if Earth spun faster,
and couldn't stop?

2
00:00:04,653 --> 00:00:06,243
You're standing
on the equator, and you'll

3
00:00:06,243 --> 00:00:07,953
watch what happens
minute by minute,

4
00:00:07,953 --> 00:00:10,003
until the planet
can't take it anymore.

5
00:00:10,653 --> 00:00:13,473
The Earth keeps its size,
its air and its water.

6
00:00:14,425 --> 00:00:17,045
Only the spin changes,
and it only gets faster.

7
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:20,055
One number matters:
the length of a day.

8
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,730
It starts
at 24 hours and ends

9
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,665
at about an hour
and 24 minutes.

10
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,475
Under it,
how fast the ground

11
00:00:26,475 --> 00:00:28,050
moves under your feet.

12
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,645
Nothing resets.

13
00:00:30,423 --> 00:00:31,523
Nothing slows.

14
00:00:32,223 --> 00:00:34,318
Treat every number
as a first guess.

15
00:00:34,825 --> 00:00:36,660
Right now the ground
carries you

16
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:39,690
at about 1,670 km/h.

17
00:00:40,382 --> 00:00:43,442
What you feel is a tiny
push outward: the spin

18
00:00:43,442 --> 00:00:45,582
makes you about a third
of a percent lighter.

19
00:00:46,393 --> 00:00:47,148
Hang on.

20
00:00:47,148 --> 00:00:49,068
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

21
00:00:49,068 --> 00:00:50,913
Okay, back to the math.

22
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:55,897
And then the spin has only
just begun to speed up.

23
00:00:56,875 --> 00:00:57,905
Part 1 of 8.
